  "question": {
    "text": "In the given circuit.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. The charge stored on capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp; ______&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cae6bf64-5e50-47a4-a6f7-fc4670e21f19.png\" style=\"width: 347px; height: 241px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the diagram of the circuit,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are in series, so the total capacitance is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are parallel, the total capacitance is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are in series. So the equivalent capacitance is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p>Using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d1ba759f-43cb-4ae0-b9ca-59765a1276c3.png\" style=\"width: 361px; height: 248px;\" /></p><p>The charge through the battery,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;From the diagram above,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#956;C</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
